945427421b1da7cdb77c677e285f6a00a94fb8d42163328e337793b3dc808"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":93476,"output_tokens":3637,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the admission report's path and fields, and add an acceptance criterion asserting each admitted criterion's selector tier is recorded there.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","E2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the selector's tier is recorded in the admission report, never on the spec'","Drift report by contrast is fully specified: path docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/drift-report.md plus recorded fields","No AC names an admission-report path or asserts tier is recorded"],"finding":"The plan references an 'admission report' as the sink for the selector's tier ('the selector's tier is recorded in the admission report, never on the spec') but never specifies its path, format, or fields, unlike the drift report which has an explicit path and enumerated fields; no acceptance criterion proves the admission report is written or that tier is recorded there.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f557c663fe80e11ca","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > Disposition (admission report clause)","norm_id":"n2786e36e4be0c34a","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must decide where the admission report lives and what it contains","Reviewer cannot verify the tier-recording claim is satisfied"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Give the admission report a concrete path (e.g. docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/admission-report.md) and enumerate its fields (criterion, prompt-id, selector tier, finalized usd), then add a pytest AC asserting a row with the expected tier is written per admitted criterion.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the crash-safe ordering that makes a criterion truly atomic — e.g. write the spec to a temp path and os.rename it into place, then finalize() the ledger, and on resume treat a ledger row WITHOUT its committed spec (or a committed spec WITHOUT a ledger row) as a reconciliation case rather than an unconditional skip.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ledger.reconcile returns the existing row for a present run_id (ledger.py:195-197), so the ledger is the sole resume/skip oracle","No-shadowing guard SKIPS 'any criterion whose <prompt-id>.eval.yaml already exists' (eval_solver load order confirmed: eval_spec_path before _packaged_eval_spec, eval.py:76-78)","The plan specifies no ordering, temp-write+rename, or reconciliation between the disk spec write and the ledger append — the two operations have a crash window the word 'atomic' papers over"],"finding":"The per-criterion atomicity claim is not actually atomic: the spec-file write to `.rebar/evals/<id>.eval.yaml` and the ledger `finalize()` append are two separate, unordered disk operations, and the crash-resume oracle is the ledger (run_id present => skip). A crash between them corrupts state in either order — ledger-first-then-crash permanently loses the spec while spend is charged; spec-first-then-crash leaves a spec that the no-shadowing SKIP guard later treats as a pre-existing built-in, so the criterion is never finalized or counted.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f954a8a1fd9bd6650","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Failure disposition: 'A criterion is atomic: spec written and spend finalize()d only after all its cases finish three runs — no partial criterion lands' and 'a re-run resumes at the first criterion absent from the ledger'","norm_id":"n33c5dc82823d48fe","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Process is killed (OOM/SIGKILL/host loss) after finalize() appends the ledger row but before the spec YAML is flushed to disk: on re-run the criterion is skipped as already-finalized, so its spec is silently never written despite counted spend","Process is killed after the spec YAML is written but before finalize(): on re-run the criterion is skipped by the no-shadowing guard because its .eval.yaml exists, so it is never finalized/counted and stays half-landed"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Make the spec YAML write the committing action: write it via temp-file + atomic rename, THEN finalize() the ledger; on resume, before skipping, cross-check that ledger row and spec file agree, re-driving (via reconcile, which won't double-charge) or repairing any criterion where exactly one of the two exists, and have the no-shadowing skip apply only to specs whose run_id is NOT in this epic's ledger.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":